# imaging_open_export.mac
# Batch-only VRML export of the full open-field imaging world (tracker + collimator +
# trigger stage, whichever is currently built) -- NO uranium (filename contains
# "imaging_open" -> Mode::kImagingOpen, which never builds the uranium slab), NO beam/
# field needed since this only draws the geometry and writes it to a VRML file. Deliberately
# does NOT contain "vis" so MAIN.cc's kVisMode check (line ~32) stays false even though it
# contains "imaging_open" -- kImagingOpen alone already forces kVisMode false, routing this
# to the plain batch-execute branch instead of an interactive Qt session.
/vis/open VRML2FILE
/vis/viewer/set/style surface
/vis/viewer/set/auxiliaryEdge true
/vis/drawVolume
/vis/viewer/flush
